llama-server-ckpt-min-head.patch, 2026-11-11. Base: llama.cpp master 7592b61d3 (tools/server/server-context.cpp only). Apply: git apply
What: LLAMA_SERVER_CKPT_MIN_HEAD=N (default 0 = stock). The chat path breaks the prompt batch at the user-message start
(message spans from the chat template) to take a context checkpoint there. With the usual short template head this is a
42-token batch. When experts live in host RAM, that batch runs MUL_MAT_ID for every host layer on the per-expert pageable
path (below LLAMA_WS_MIN_TOKENS), then takes a checkpoint sync and an exposed PLE prep. With N > 0, no break and no
checkpoint are taken at a user start within the first N tokens; later checkpoints (near the end) are unchanged.
Measured (RTX 5090, a MoE GGUF (IQ1_M), -ncmoe 12 -t 8 -b 4096 -ub 4096 --cache-ram 0, LLAMA_WS_PIN_GIB=8, on top of
llama-pinned-copy-stream v2 + llama-moe-prefill, cold chat text, 3 reps x 2 passes, wall tok/s):
  10k: 4,551 [4,544-4,561] -> 5,278 [5,268-5,294] (+16%);  2.7k: 3,089 [2,760-3,129] -> 4,731 [4,412-4,741] (+53%)
Outputs: not bitwise (the batch boundaries move). The first argmax divergences are near-ties (top-2 probabilities within
0.01-0.09), the same envelope as stock -ub 2048 vs -ub 4096. Checkpoint restore still works (cache_n 2215 on divergent
follow-ups).
Evidence: boltbeam-runs/llama-expert-table-20261111.md (Lever "why 1.4x"), run dir boltbeam-runs/llama-expert-table-20261111/

